# RIINA Language Rules for Cursor AI

You are writing code in RIINA, a formally verified language with Bahasa Melayu keywords.

## File Extension
.rii

## Syntax Essentials
- Functions: `fungsi name(param: Type) -> ReturnType kesan Effect { body }`
- Let bindings: `biar name = value;` (semicolons required)
- If/else: `kalau condition { ... } lain { ... }` (else required)
- Match: `padan value { pattern => result, _ => default }`
- Effects: Declare with `kesan`. Pure=`Bersih`, IO=`Tulis`/`Baca`
- Secrets: `Rahsia<T>` — cannot be printed. Use `dedah` to declassify.
- Pipe: `value |> f1 |> f2`
- Entry: `fungsi utama() -> Nombor kesan Tulis { ... pulang 0; }`

## Keywords (Bahasa Melayu | English)
fungsi|fn, biar|let, ubah|mut, kalau|if, lain|else, untuk|for,
selagi|while, pulang|return, padan|match, rahsia|secret, dedah|declassify,
kesan|effect, laku|perform, kendali|handle, sulit|classify, bukti|prove,
bentuk|struct, pilihan|enum, sifat|trait, laksana|impl, awam|pub

## Types
Nombor(Int), Teks(String), Benar(Bool), Kosong(Unit),
Rahsia<T>(Secret), Bukti<T>(Proof), Senarai<T>(List), Mungkin<T>(Option)

## Effects (in order)
Bersih(0) < Ubah(1) < Baca(2) < Peruntuk(3) < Tulis(4) < SistemFail(5) < Rangkaian(6) < Kripto(8) < Sistem(10) < Masa(11)

## Security Levels
Awam < Dalaman < Sesi < Pengguna < Sistem < Rahsia

## Style
- snake_case for functions/variables (Bahasa Melayu preferred)
- PascalCase for types
- 4-space indent
- Always use Bahasa Melayu keywords
